We are looking for a technically excellent corporate lawyer with experience in corporate finance, M&A (domestic and cross-border) and private equity (beneficial, but not essential). The ideal candidate will have trained at a large South African or international firm and will have had exposure to top-tier corporate/M&A work. Experience in public company work would be beneficial but is not essential.
In addition to having excellent technical skills, candidates will be commercially aware, with a strong knowledge of corporate activity and trends in the South African and regional markets. Pinsent Masons is a collegiate, barrier-free work environment and candidates should be able to demonstrate a strong history of teamwork and a client-focussed approach. Candidates will also have excellent communication and project management skills.
The successful candidate will be:
a team player who wants significant responsibility and to take ownership of matters with strong support from senior and junior team members;
interested in developing strong working relationships with colleagues and willing to contribute to the development of junior team members;
be technically excellent and want to be a subject matter expert;
exercise common sense and good commercial judgement;
be innovative and receptive to different ways of working in a fresh and fast-paced environment, including a willingness to contribute to various aspects of the team's practice and client relationships;
have strong inter-personal skills and be comfortable with client-facing responsibilities; and
have an interest in being part of an international practice with a global outlook that does things differently.
